-# wordpress_wedding
\ No newline at end of file
+# Adaptive Website Testing Tool
+
+A lightweight SPA for testing how a URL renders across common device sizes at the same time.
+
+## Included MVP Features
+
+- URL input with normalization (`https://` auto-prepended).
+- Four required presets:
+  - Desktop `1920×1080`
+  - Laptop `1366×768`
+  - Tablet `768×1024`
+  - Mobile `375×812`
+- Grid view (2×2), single view, and split view.
+- iframe-based viewport rendering with fixed dimensions.
+- Global zoom slider (`25%` to `200%`) and auto-fit.
+- Reload all active iframes.
+- Orientation toggle for tablet/mobile (and custom device).
+- Optional overlays:
+  - viewport width
+  - breakpoint label
+  - grid visualization
+- Optional custom device resolution.
+- Graceful iframe restriction fallback via “Open in new tab”.
+
+## Run
+
+Because this project is plain HTML/CSS/JS, you can run it with any static server.
+
+Example:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m http.server 4173
+```
+
+Then open:
+
+- <http://localhost:4173>
+
+## Notes
+
+- Some sites cannot be embedded in iframes due to `X-Frame-Options` or CSP `frame-ancestors` policies.
+- Scroll sync is best-effort and constrained by browser same-origin policies.
+
+## Downloadable Archive
+
+Archive file name in repo root:
+
+- `adaptive-website-testing-tool.zip`
+
+### How to download
+
+If you already cloned the repo locally:
+
+```bash
+cp adaptive-website-testing-tool.zip ~/Downloads/
+```
+
+If you use GitHub web UI:
+
+1. Open `adaptive-website-testing-tool.zip` in the repository root.
+2. Click **Download** (or use the **Raw** button and save the file).
+
+If needed, create/recreate the archive locally:
+
+```bash
+zip -r adaptive-website-testing-tool.zip README.md index.html styles.css app.js
+```
